                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the Persian language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Persian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbd18571-43f4-30bc-8352-406e792553b3",
                                        "entry_id": "1cabd830-e7cf-396b-b8e9-b5baa12744f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to Persius (Roman writer)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0c753ab-6a4f-419f-a508-0c8159722d3b",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd18571-43f4-30bc-8352-406e792553b3",
                                                "text": "...as it seems from an Ovidian or Persian standpoint and also, perhaps, from the comic standpoints of Plautus or Caecilius..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "de958204-129f-4e31-a445-22d0fdcd4672",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7a974bb-dcd7-3c9a-95a4-7eb5ea1ff583",
                        "target_lang_word": "Farsi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Farsi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c3e6cfc-8cb0-31ce-889d-0c2e1f146842",
                                        "entry_id": "a758138b-6bbe-3a44-99ef-895871b98b32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of Persian (“The Persian language”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "proscribed"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c332163-1a2c-4b8d-a202-1f963b8274e0",
                                                "sense_id": "4c3e6cfc-8cb0-31ce-889d-0c2e1f146842",
                                                "text": "That the Farsi or Persian is not a language derived from the Pehlevi, but a collateral and independent tongue, seems to be sufficiently certain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd7813ec-09ff-46f0-ac62-c624960489dc",
                                                "sense_id": "4c3e6cfc-8cb0-31ce-889d-0c2e1f146842",
                                                "text": "In July 1984, Radio Iran Toilers began broadcasting in Farsi from Afghanistan; by the end of 1988 it was transmitting twenty-one hours a week."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99ca5631-37ea-4c3d-87df-b13dd5104dd5",
                                                "sense_id": "4c3e6cfc-8cb0-31ce-889d-0c2e1f146842",
                                                "text": "The method of writing Farsi is logical, although reading can be trickier, as one has to guess at the unwritten consonants of unfamiliar words."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afe6759d-ea53-48e2-8227-2bb354b90f0b",
                                                "sense_id": "4c3e6cfc-8cb0-31ce-889d-0c2e1f146842",
                                                "text": "We chatted away in Farsi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d84d9fcb-d908-472a-a171-43a3c8c60ff5",
                                                "sense_id": "4c3e6cfc-8cb0-31ce-889d-0c2e1f146842",
                                                "text": "For instance, in Farsi pošt means 'back' (noun) as in pošt=am dard mikonad 'my back hurts' […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a21a855-34b1-31b1-b1f1-ab1fd634ed10",
                                        "entry_id": "a758138b-6bbe-3a44-99ef-895871b98b32",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Iranian Persian, as opposed to Dari (Afghan Persian) and Tajik (Tajik Persian)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "proscribed"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
